      "id": 1,
      "text": "Six unmarried brothers named Joseph, Trigg, Newt, Warner, John, and Richard Jett founded the community of Jet in the former Cherokee Outlet.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jet%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Warner Jett served as the first postmaster for the town of Jet.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jet%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Jet incorporated as a town in 1900 after growing from a small community established by the Jett brothers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jet%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Frisco Townsite Company relocated Jet about two miles west of its original location between 1905 and 1906.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jet%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "By August 1907, Jet featured seven general stores, two banks, two hotels, and four different denominations of churches.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jet%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
